WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.234
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.634
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.067
I appreciate it.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.534
Well, guys, tonight
in Washington, D.C.,

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:11.968
President Biden attended

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:15.167
the 99th annual National
Christmas Tree Lighting.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.601
Meanwhile the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree was like,

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:21.901
"Uh, yeah, sure, that's
the national Christmas tree."

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.334
And this was special.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:26.133
A real-life Elf on the Shelf
made an appearance.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.701
Yeah, he got up and said,

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.367
"For the last time,
my name is Pete Buttigieg."

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.501
Then organizers said,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.200
"Sorry. Here's the real
Elf on the Shelf."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.501
And then he got up and said,
"I'm sorry. For the last time,

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.467
my name is Dr. Fauci."
This is terrible.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.968
Who's writing these?
That's right.

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.367
By all accounts,
it was a great time.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.667
I mean, it definitely
went better

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.834
than Boris Johnson's
tree lighting in the U.K.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.167
This is real. Look at this.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:55.133
-Five, four, three, two, one!

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.300
-Aww.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:05.434
-"Yea-- Ohh.
All right. Go home, everybody."

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.901
Let's get to some news.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.534
Earlier today, President Biden
revealed his plan to fight COVID

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:14.300
this winter, which includes
free at-home testing,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.033
a public education campaign,
and no lockdowns.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.667
And everyone was like,
"Let's not rule out

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.067
day drinking so fast."

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:24.234
I mean, that's --

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:25.734
That's right. No lockdowns.

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:26.934
Biden must have felt the glare

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.834
of a million brides
planning their wedding.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:32.634
Like, "Don't you dare.
Don't you dare."

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.701
Biden's plan
also extends the mandate

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:38.167
requiring people to wear masks
on public transit.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.334
Then people riding the New
York City subway here were like,

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.834
"Yeah, can you also require
a mandate to wear pants?

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.834
Because masks are, like,

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.767
eighth on the list
of what's happening here."

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:50.234
[ Applause ]

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:52.634
"Ohh! Applesauce."

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.434
-"Don't grab the pole!"

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:58.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.767
-But Biden did lay out
an ambitious goal.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.834
By springtime, he wants
the majority of Americans

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.367
to know
how to pronounce "omicron."

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.934
-It's called the omnicron.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:10.200
Omnicron. Omnicron.
The omnicron variant.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.200
-Ombicrombie and Fitch.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.434
I read that President Trump

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.367
might have tried
to self-publish his memoir

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.501
to avoid getting
a smaller advance

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.601
than President Obama
got for his memoir.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:25.467
Yeah, and Trump
is even considering

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.234
a few titles for his book.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.501
For example...

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:31.033
-Oh, here we go.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.534
-What's up, Mark?
-Let me guess.

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:34.901
You're gonna make fun of Trump

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.267
by saying a bunch
of fake book titles.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.868
-I mean, yeah,
that was the plan.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.334
-Oh, let me guess.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.367
And then each cover
will pop up on the screen,

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.200
and people will see it
and laugh about it.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.834
-Right. We often show graphics

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.534
during the monologue
to make our audience laugh.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:52.167
-Man, I know exactly
how this will go down.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:55.367
You'll start off with something
like, "Tweet Pray Love."

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:57.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah, then you'll

00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:01.000
follow it up with,
"Oh, the Places You'll Riot!"

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.634
-Yeah, then you'll do,
"Are You There Vlad?

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:05.634
It's me, Donald."
-Yeah.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.100
-Oh, oh, and after that,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.000
you're gonna do,
"Fifty Shades of COVID."

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.667
-Yep. Yeah, these are all
pretty good examples. Yeah.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.200
-Oh, and then you'll do one

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.100
that says,
"Lord of the Onion Rings."

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.300
-Wait, wait. No, no.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.701
You'll do, "From Whom
the Taco Bell Tolls."

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.267
And then instead of "Clifford
the Big Red Dog," you'll do,

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.133
"Clip-On the Big Red Tie."
-Yeah, I know.

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:29.400
But these are -- We probably
wouldn't do this many.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.234
But, yeah,
these are all great examples.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.467
-Oh, then you'll do,

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:35.100
"Nineteen Eighty
Four Seasons Total Landscaping."

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.434
-Yeah, exactly.
-Or a couple where you don't

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.501
even have to change
the title like,

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:42.934
"Pride and Prejudice"
or "Eclipse."

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:44.467
-Ah! Whoa, whoa.

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.567
And then you'll finish it off
with something classic like...

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.801
-"The Color Orange."

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.667
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.200
-Is that how
it's gonna go down, Jimbo?

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.000
-Yeah, yeah.
You guys nailed it. That was it.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.767
Yeah.
-That sounds like a fun bit.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.067
You should do it.

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:02.400
-All right.
We'll do it tomorrow.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.767
Thank you.

